From 00ed616da1d4067cc9bd5097d63a8d4610af58a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Malard <malard@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 19:14:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [buildsteps][depends] Keep built depends of other revisions
 in a workspace cache

Each Jenkins job builds in one workspace per agent, and prepare-depends
throws the whole depends build away whenever the last commit touching
tools/depends differs from the one it was built for. master and Piers
have different tools/depends histories, so every switch between a
master PR and a Piers PR rebuilds depends from scratch, and so does the
switch back.

On the Apple jobs that turns a 5-9 minute build into a 30-37 minute
one. In the 2026-10-05 PR builds, every OSX-64 and TVOS build that
followed a build for the other branch took 30-35 minutes, and the next
build for the same branch took about 8. BuildMulti-PR builds one PR at
a time, so each switch delays the whole PR queue by that much, twice.

When the depends hash changes, prepare-depends now moves the untracked
files of a tagged (fully built) tools/depends into
$WORKSPACE/.build-cache, keyed by the hash it was built for, and moves
a cached build for the new hash back into place if there is one. Moves
stay on the same filesystem, so a switch costs seconds. The cache only
ever holds builds that reached tagSuccessFulBuild in make-depends, and
the rest of the workspace is still cleaned exactly as before.

BUILD_CACHE_ENTRIES (default 2) caps the number of other revisions
kept; the oldest are deleted first. 0 deletes the cache and restores
the previous behaviour.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
